WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.300
So here's the record.

2
00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:04.768
Every notice from every
provider becomes one record,

3
00:00:04.768 --> 00:00:06.975
defined in the kit's JSON schema.

4
00:00:06.975 --> 00:00:10.425
It has an ID made of the provider
and the provider's own ID,

5
00:00:10.425 --> 00:00:12.975
which is what the router de-duplicates on.

6
00:00:12.975 --> 00:00:17.470
It has one of six kinds, a status,
plain-text title and summary,

7
00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:22.975
the impact window in UTC, and the
services, regions and resources it names.

8
00:00:22.975 --> 00:00:27.768
The three action fields matter most:
whether action is needed, by when,

9
00:00:27.768 --> 00:00:32.225
and who said so, the provider's own
field or a stated rule of the kit.

10
00:00:32.225 --> 00:00:33.890
And it ends with a fingerprint.
